# Copy to .env.local (never committed). Placeholders only.
# API reached through the same-origin proxy in next.config.ts; read at dev start and at build time:
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000
# Set only to bypass the proxy and call the API directly from the browser:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=<https://api.example/v1>
# Supabase Auth for sellers (spec §2). Without these the dashboard runs open, for local work.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=<https://your-project.supabase.co>
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from the Supabase dashboard>
# Server-only: the secret the API proxy sends with the visitor's address (the API's
# VISITOR_PROXY_SECRET). In production a Worker secret: `pnpm exec wrangler secret put
# VISITOR_PROXY_SECRET`, never in a build file. Unset locally: the API counts the caller.
# VISITOR_PROXY_SECRET=<the same random value as the API's>
# Development builds only (ignored by `pnpm build`): a token from `make dev-token SUB=dev`
# lets local mode call the API without Supabase.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_ACCESS_TOKEN=<output of make dev-token>
